   "source": "pymupdf4llm",
   "text": "**Characteristics** (Table 6, Figure 21) Stem: shape in cross\nsection round. Leaf: type pinnate, number of leaflets three\nto seven, margin entire, colour of upper side in relation to\ncolour of lower side same, hairiness of lower side absent to",
   "text_format": "markdown",
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "bbox": null,
   "confidence": null,
   "id": "e17",
   "page": 1,
   "signal": "markdown-syntax",
   "source": "pymupdf4llm",
   "text": "very weak, hairiness of upper side absent to very weak,\ntexture of upper side warty. Flowering stem: position of\nflowers axillary. Inflorescence: number of flowers one.\nFlower: shape closed bell. Petal: main colour white (RHS\n155C), secondary colour red, position of secondary colour\npredominantly on midrib, prominence of midvein weak.\nStigma: colour greyed-red, swelling present. Anther:\ncolour greyed-red. (RHS 139A), colour lower side yellowgreen (RHS 147B. (Note: All RHS colour chart numbers\nrefer to 2001 edition.)",
   "text_format": "markdown",
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "bbox": null,
   "confidence": null,
   "id": "e18",
   "page": 1,
   "signal": "markdown-syntax",
   "source": "pymupdf4llm",
   "text": "**Origin and Breeding** Spontaneous mutation: from\n_Boronia heterophylla_ at owners property in Tauranga, New\nZealand in 1995. The parental form is characterised by\npink flowers. A mutant was selected for further",
